    {
      "formation_id": "ATTRACTION_SCAN_148-F1",
      "title": "Remote overseas actors with bounded non-specialist China-side physical tasks -> replaceable local executors who can follow a checklist and return evidence",
      "seed_kind": "BROAD_REALITY_PATTERN",
      "evidence_class": "REPEATED_REMOTE_TO_LOCAL_PHYSICAL_EXECUTION",
      "evidence_summary": "Multiple current providers independently expose the same broad pattern: a client outside the location needs a person physically present in China for a bounded task such as pickup, handoff, simple visit, visible-condition capture or appointment coordination, and expects an evidence record afterward. The retained edge is deliberately narrower than factory inspection, certified audit, regulated representation, purchasing custody or specialist field service. Existing supply is fragmented into agency-style providers; this scan has not yet proven that one exact general-purpose network owns the low-risk checklist-to-evidence control loop.",
